      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The author analyzes the importance of pain as a defense mechanism against a noxious stimulus; its sensory-discriminatory, affective-emotional, cognitive and behavior components; and how the transmission of pain impulses by means of peripheral receptors occur; neuronal ways of conduction; and the reception and interpretation of pain. The author also states the objectives nurses have in treating pain."},
